course: dictionary
lesson: 3382
title: Big words about big questions
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words are about the biggest questions people ask. Existential comes from existence, which means the fact of being alive or real. «Existential questions are big questions about life and why we are here; almost everyone wonders about them sometimes.» So an existential question is a question about the meaning of life.
explain: Look at the context clues: big questions and why we are here. Those words show the topic is life and its meaning, not an everyday problem like where your shoes are. Try the swap: "a question about the meaning of life" fits the sentence, so your meaning works.
explain: Existential can also describe a threat. An existential threat is one that could end something completely, such as a species, a country or the world. The word threat is a clue that it is a danger, and existential tells you how serious it is.
explain: People sometimes joke about having an existential crisis over something small, like a lost sock. This is informal and meant as a joke. When you are not sure what a word means, check a dictionary.
fact: Existential means to do with existence, or the fact of being real and alive.
fact: «Existential questions» are big questions about why we exist and what life means.
fact: «Existential threat» means a danger that could end something completely.
fact: An «existential crisis» is a time when someone worries deeply about the meaning of their life, and people often use the phrase jokingly.
exercise: «Why am I here?» is an example of which kind of question? | A question about sums | A question about spelling | A question about the weather | *An existential question
exercise: In the news, climate change may be called an existential threat. What does that mean? | It is a new kind of sports game | *It could end something completely | It is a small problem that is easy to fix | It is only about cold weather
exercise: Maya jokes, «I am having an existential crisis about my socks.» What does this joke suggest? | She has been to a philosophy class | *She is joking about something small | She is worried that the world will end | She is worried about the meaning of life
test: Which is the best meaning of existential? | To do with sport and games | To do with cooking food | To do with money | *To do with existence and the big questions about life
test: Which sentence uses existential correctly? | We played an existential game of tag | I ate an existential sandwich for lunch | *Scientists warned that the disease was an existential threat to the species | My existential bike is very fast
exam: Which question is an existential question? | What colour is the sky? | *What is the point of life? | Where did I put my pencil? | What is 5 times 6?
